    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math>&nbsp;be a function defined as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math> is the greatest integer less than or equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;exists, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
